  "authority": {
    "document": "Open Design Specification for .dwg files v5.4.1 section 20.4.44",
    "qualification": "The specification describes the R14 byte as unknown and observed zero; the nonzero ODA-produced control is bounded contrary empirical evidence, not a replacement for the specification."
  },
  "observations": [
    "Two R2000 DXF seeds were authored locally with matching root dictionary, line, named dictionary and XRECORD; their selected hard-ownership flag differs (0 versus 1).",
    "ODA 27.1.0 produced R13 and R14 DWGs from each seed and reopened each to R2000 ASCII DXF. LibreDWG 0.14 supplied the independent peer object model; a separate bit walker checked dictionary frame size, CRC, body boundary, entry names and handle roles, and next-frame CRC.",
    "For the R13 pair, the ordinary DICTIONARY has no R14 byte; its ACAD APPID-bound EED contains TREAT_AS_HARD with value 0 or 1. The selected dictionary frames differ in one physical byte.",
    "For the R14 pair, selected dictionary frames likewise differ in one physical byte, decoded by the walker as the R14-only byte 0 or 1. LibreDWG reports corresponding is_hardowner values.",
    "ODA reopen preserves the two ownership flags, the named entry, owner links and XRECORD values. Physical DXF entry codes are 350 for 0 and 360 for 1; ezdxf independently reads the selected graph and values.",
    "Candidate strict conversion refuses all four controls without replacing the destination. R13 stops at the ModelDocViewStyle cross-version guard; R14 reports incomplete source disposition because the generated file contains an unsupported class."
  ],
